## Concept Overview
Dynamic programming optimizes recursive problems by caching subproblem results. In React, useMemo prevents expensive recalculations during re-renders.

## Implementation Details
### Top-Down Memoization (Recursive)
```javascript
const fibonacci = useMemo(() => {
  const memo = {};
  const fib = (n) => {
    if (n in memo) return memo[n];
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    memo[n] = fib(n - 1) + fib(n - 2);
    return memo[n];
  };
  return fib;
}, []);
```

### Bottom-Up Tabulation (Iterative)
```javascript
const fibonacci = useMemo(() => {
  return (n) => {
    if (n <= 1) return n;
    let prev = 0, curr = 1;
    for (let i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
      [prev, curr] = [curr, prev + curr];
    }
    return curr;
  };
}, []);
```

## Common Pitfalls
- **Dependency array**: Empty array [] ensures function isn't recreated
- **Memory leaks**: Large memo objects can cause memory issues
- **Over-optimization**: useMemo overhead may exceed benefits for simple calculations
- **Referential equality**: useMemo preserves function reference for child components

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests mastery of closures, Promise coordination, and cache invalidation patterns in JavaScript without DOM dependencies.

## Key Concepts
- Closures for maintaining per-URL cache state
- Promise deduplication for concurrent in-flight requests
- Stale-while-revalidate caching strategy
- Race condition prevention and cache lifecycle management

## Code Example
```javascript
function makeFetcher() {
  const cache = new Map();
  return {
    fetchMemo: (url, ttlMs) => {
      const getEntry = () => cache.get(url) || { value: null, ts: 0, inFlight: null };
      const fetchAndUpdate = async () => {
        try {
          const response = await fetch(url);
          const data = await response.json();
          cache.set(url, { value: data, ts: Date.now(), inFlight: null });
          return data;
        } catch (error) {
          const entry = getEntry();
          entry.inFlight = null;
          throw error;
        }
      };

      return {
        get: async () => {
          const entry = getEntry();
          const now = Date.now();
          const isFresh = entry.value && (now - entry.ts) < ttlMs;

          if (isFresh) return entry.value;

          if (entry.inFlight) {
            await entry.inFlight;
            return getEntry().value;
          }

          if (entry.value) {
            entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
            return entry.value;
          }

          entry.inFlight = fetchAndUpdate();
          return await entry.inFlight;
        },
        invalidate: () => cache.delete(url)
      };
    }
  };
}
```

